The client waits out the parse: a client whose zygote was alive but had yet to
bind waited ten seconds and then ran its cold command, so a parse that staged a
cold cache for longer than that got a second parser beside it, staging the same
slots into the same directory. The wait now ends with the zygote's life, not
with a count.

